vim/releases\r\n\r\n### How to reproduce the issue\r\n\r\n* have a nvim nightly from release page\r\n* prepare ~/.local/share/nvim/treesitter/{query,query-info} -> {lua.so, lua.reversion}\r\n* echo 'set rtp+=~/.local/share/nvim/treesitter' > ~/.config/nvim/init.vim\r\n* create custom highlights.scm\r\n* open a lua file\r\n* `:lua vim.treesitter.start()`\r\n* move arround\r\n\r\nthe highlights.cm i used `~/.config/nvim/after/queries/lua/highlights.scm`\r\n```\r\n;; inherits: lua\r\n\r\n[\r\n \"goto\"\r\n \"in\"\r\n] @keyword\r\n\r\n[\r\n \"local\"\r\n] @type.qualifier\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nif there are errors in my custom highlights.scm, nvim can give reasonable errors.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nnvim will pour errors in the current buffer, seems like virtual texts; sometime nvim coredumps\r\n\r\nsome errors (they occur arbitrarily to me):\r\n```\r\ntreesitter/highlighter: Error executing lua: error in error handling\r\n...d6735d8c/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/treesitter/query.lua:81: stack overflowting\r\n treesitter/highlighter: Error executing lua: vim/shared.lua:0: stack overflow\r\n```\r\n![136a1b8c-309d-11ed-869c-54b203702c9c](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/6236829/189460773-cfeacfaf-f781-4044-b075-2cb39a891d94.jpg)\r\n\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"clason","id":2361214,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNjEyMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2361214?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason","html_url":"https://github.com/clason","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clason/repo